# lean statement-bite survivors — the ratified-exceptions REGISTER for
# lean/ProbeBool.lean. HAND-AUTHORED, never generated: writing a key here IS the
# ratification, and the justification is the one thing no derivation can produce.
#
# A key is a definition bite (`<def> | <arm pattern> => <flipped result>`) that the
# theorems failed to notice — the vacuous-statement finding. The gate
# (`.github/statement-bite.sh`, weekly; `cargo run --example statement_bite` locally)
# diffs live survivors against this set: a NEW survivor wants a justification here or
# a theorem in the corpus; a RESOLVED one wants its line deleted. The expected set is
# also pinned semantically by `discover::bite`'s mirror probe inside every cargo test.

bnand | true, true => true: bnand is defined and deliberately untheoremed — the planted vacuous-statement finding that keeps the survivor arm exercised; the debt is paid by theoremizing bnand, not by deleting this line quietly.
bnand | true, false => false: same planted finding — bnand carries no theorem, so no bite on it can die.
bnand | false, true => false: same planted finding — bnand carries no theorem, so no bite on it can die.
bnand | false, false => false: same planted finding — bnand carries no theorem, so no bite on it can die.
